course: dictionary
lesson: 580
title: One word, three meanings: auto
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word auto can mean three different things. Context clues tell you which one. Ask: is the sentence about a car, a machine setting, or the start of a longer word?
explain: For a car, look for «auto repair shop». Mainly Americans say auto for car, so you will hear it most in the USA. Here auto is a thing you can name.
explain: For a setting, look at «Set the camera to auto». The camera is a machine, and auto means it chooses its settings by itself. Test it: «Set the camera to automatic» still makes sense, so auto means automatic here.
explain: For the start of a word, look for auto- followed by more letters. «auto- means self (autobiography, automatic)». An autobiography is the story of your own life, written by you. When you see auto- at the start, look for the meaning self or by itself.
fact: Auto (noun) means a car, mainly in American English: «auto repair shop».
fact: «Auto» is short for «automatic»: a machine does something by itself, as in «on auto».
fact: The prefix auto- means self or by itself.
fact: Examples of auto-words: autograph, autopilot, automobile, autobiography.
fact: Context clues, and a quick swap test, help you find the right meaning of auto.
exercise: «The auto repair shop fixed our car.» What does auto mean here? | A setting that works by itself | *A car | A story about a life | Self
exercise: «Set the camera to auto.» What does auto mean here? | Self | *Automatic, the machine chooses by itself | A car | A map
exercise: In autobiography, what does auto- mean? | Three | Again | *Self, by itself | Two
test: «My uncle works in an auto shop in Texas.» What does auto mean here? | *A car | Self | Automatic setting | Wrongly
test: Which word is a story about your own life, written by yourself? | *Autobiography | Autopilot | Automobile | Autocorrect
exam: Ben reads «The phone will autosave your game.» What does auto mean here? | *Automatic, the phone saves by itself | A story about your life | A car | Two or three
